== G. Follow controller ownership: Pod -> Job -> JobSet ==
Discovery -[#1565C0]> Reader : [call] Cached(Pod pod-1 / p10)
Reader --[#388E3C]> Discovery : [result] full Pod; controller owner Job job-1
Discovery -[#7B1FA2]> Discovery : [decision] validate name / namespace / UID / requested RV\nappend Pod to Path; accept one controller owner
Discovery -[#1565C0]> Reader : [call] Cached(Job job-1)
Reader --[#388E3C]> Discovery : [result] no full Job watch object in this example
Discovery -[#1565C0]> Reader : [call] GetMetadata(Job demo/train-worker-0, UID job-1)
alt matching fresh metadata exists from earlier work / priming
  Reader --[#388E3C]> Discovery : [result] copied metadata; UID / RV / controller owner
else metadata read required
  Reader -[#7B1FA2]> Reader : [decision] map GVK/scope; coalesce concurrent GETs for key\nrecord read revision and start time
  Reader -[#1565C0]> API : [call] GET PartialObjectMetadata for Job\nrequest timeout bounded
  alt server accepts metadata representation
    API --[#388E3C]> Reader : [result] Job job-1 / j7; controller JobSet js-1
  else server rejects metadata representation (406 / 415)
    API --[#388E3C]> Reader : [result] 406 / 415 representation error
    Reader -[#1565C0]> API : [call] fallback full-object GET
    API --[#388E3C]> Reader : [result] full Job; retain only metadata
  end
  Reader -[#7B1FA2]> Reader : [decision] reject elapsed TTL / changed in-flight revision\notherwise cache metadata with read-start expiry
  Reader --[#388E3C]> Discovery : [result] Job metadata or stale / API error
end
Discovery -[#7B1FA2]> Discovery : [decision] verify expected job-1; append Job j7 to Path
Discovery -[#1565C0]> Reader : [call] Cached(JobSet js-1)
Reader --[#388E3C]> Discovery : [result] full JobSet js-1 / s5 with no controller owner
Discovery -[#7B1FA2]> Discovery : [decision] terminal boundary found; append JobSet\nRoot=JobSet js-1; Path=[Pod p10, Job j7, JobSet s5]
Discovery --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] GenericWorkload{Root, full Path, resolved}
note over Discovery,Reader
No controller owner ends the path. Non-controller ownerReferences are not traversed.
An explicitly ignored next-owner GVK stops at the current object: ignored_owner.
A missing owner, UID mismatch, cycle or path over 1024 objects does not invent a root.
Kubernetes scope determines whether the next GET uses demo or empty namespace.
end note

== H. Confirm the root representation and register path dependencies ==
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Inventory : [call] Lookup(discovered root GroupKind)
Inventory --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] JobSet definition selects v1alpha2 representation
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Runtime : [call] ensure full JobSet watch exists\ncreate dynamic root watch if this kind was not planned
opt dynamically discovered root kind lacks a full observation
  Runtime -[#1565C0]> API : [call] full root resource LIST/WATCH
  API --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [event] root object available; enqueue resolution again
end
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Reader : [call] verify complete path evidence and input Pod RV
Reader --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] matching identities and available path evidence\ninput Pod RV unchanged
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] confirm root remains terminal across known versions\nreject conflicting owner-bearing alias
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] attach pod-1 to root js-1; replace old attachment if moved\nindex every path object -> dependent Pod / root
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Runtime : [call] mark pod-1 dirty; queue root js-1 after 20ms
note over Runtime,Inventory
A definition chooses interpretation after ownership determines the root.
It does not stop traversal merely because an intermediate Job has a Karta.
Unknown non-Pod roots can still have generic ownership rows and creation time.
A standalone Pod without a Karta is excluded by this implementation.
end note

== I. A root with zero Pods uses the same root calculation ==
API --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [event] JobSet root from selected-definition watch\npossibly before any Pod exists
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Discovery : [call] Get(JobSet ref)
Discovery -[#1565C0]> Reader : [call] Cached(JobSet ref); inspect controller owner
Reader --[#388E3C]> Discovery : [result] terminal JobSet
Discovery --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] Path=[JobSet]; same Root js-1
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] create / refresh rootState and enqueue root key
note over Runtime,Store
Zero Pods does not imply Undefined or absence of the workload.
A known root can publish creation and normalized status with an empty PodPages list.
Pod mapping work is skipped when there are no attached Pods.
end note

== J. Snapshot inputs and prepare separate creation / interpretation proofs ==
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Store : [call] Published(js-1)
Store --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] previous immutable publication, if any
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] under lock capture root generation, dirty Pods,\nKarta origin, global/kind definition keys and root failures
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] full refresh if needed; otherwise copy only dirty Pod state\nrelease Runtime lock for evaluation
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Reader : [call] Cached(selected JobSet representation)\nread current full root object and evidence
Reader --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] JobSet s5; root object proof and expiry
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] objectSelector + resource inclusion/exclusion rules\nremove publication if root is excluded
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] Creation = root evidence + root-generation dependency\nStatus = Creation + global/kind definition + Karta-source evidence
note over Runtime,Store
Definition failure can invalidate interpretation without erasing independently proven creation time.
Merged evidence takes the earliest expiry and all required dependencies.
Pod mapping additionally requires its complete ownership path and Pod proof.
end note

== K. Evaluate workload status from the full JobSet object ==
Runtime -[#1565C0]> SDK : [call] prepareWorkload(Karta, full JobSet s5)\nStructureSummary + ComponentFactoryFromObject
SDK -[#7B1FA2]> SDK : [decision] factory creates named components and owner links\nall component spec/status accessors bind this JobSet object
Runtime -[#1565C0]> SDK : [call] GetRootComponent().GetStatus(ctx)
SDK -[#1565C0]> SDK : [call] Accessor.ExtractStatus(StatusDefinition)\nread JobSet .status.conditions
note right of SDK
Example JobSet input:
replicatedJobsStatus =
[{name: worker, active: 2,
  ready: 0, failed: 0}]
conditions = []
end note
SDK -[#1565C0]> SDK : [call] run configured JQ matchers on JobSet JSON\nInitializing expression -> true\nRunning expression -> true
SDK -[#7B1FA2]> SDK : [decision] OR matchers within a status; AND their clauses\ncollect every matching status, not first match
SDK --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] MatchedStatuses=[Running, Initializing]\nHasStatus=true; both phases are retained
note over Runtime,SDK
The exporter does not sum Pod phases or child Job states into workload status.
JobSet's own controller already wrote the counts and conditions on the root.
Successful evaluation with no matches yields Undefined. No StatusDefinition yields no status series.
JQ/extraction failure is evaluation_failed, not an application Failed phase.
end note

== L. Resolve workload-status labels before the Pod loop ==
