note over Runtime,SDK
The child component has Kind=Job, but its spec accessor still reads the JobSet.
Pod selectors read the Pod through a separate PodQuerier.
replica_group_id comes from ReplicaSelector, not GangScheduling group-by fields.
A missing required instance or invalid selector result is a mapping error.
end note

Runtime -[#1565C0]> Labels : [call] resolve(karta_pod_workload_info, full Pod)
loop sources in configured order; example [pod, workload]
  Labels -[#1565C0]> Labels : [call] evaluate CEL on chosen object\nPod team=batch; workload team=platform
  Labels -[#7B1FA2]> Labels : [decision] first nonempty string wins: team=batch\nempty value tries next source
end
Labels --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] custom label map; separate error map
note over Runtime,Labels
Workload results are cached for this immutable root object across metrics and Pods.
Pod evaluation uses the current Pod. Rules compile once, outside reconciliation.
An error can be retained even if a later source succeeds: report evaluation_failed health.
Cancellation aborts the call. Bad / absent custom labels do not become an application phase.
end note

== N. Build rows and atomically reject superseded calculations ==
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] combine mapping evidence; cache evaluated Pod result\nand its mapping error reason\nreuse only with compatible definition / root generation / Pod RV
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Store : [call] build immutable sorted PodPages\nfull BuildPodPages or WithPod for dirty rows
Store --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] new pages; share unchanged pages (max 256 rows/page)
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] reacquire lock: same root state + generation?\nsame global/kind keys + lookup success + Karta origin/GVK?
Runtime -[#1565C0]> Reader : [call] check selected full root RV and active proof keys\nfor evidence without a failure reason
Reader --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] matching root and active dependencies, or stale
Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] rootBoundaryLocked under Reader read lock\nwhen not publishing an existing root failure
alt any commit guard changed
  Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] discard calculation; restore drained dirty work\nreturn ErrStale; queue retries
else all commit guards pass
  Runtime -[#1565C0]> Store : [call] Publish(Publication for js-1)
  Store -[#7B1FA2]> Store : [decision] swap root record and dependency references under Store lock
  Store --[#388E3C]> Runtime : [result] publication visible atomically
  Runtime -[#7B1FA2]> Runtime : [decision] save compatible caches; schedule renewal before proof expiry
end
note over Runtime,Store
Publishing transfers ownership of nested maps and slices. They remain immutable.
An old computation cannot make a new source generation valid.
These guards are concurrency protection, not a second ownership discovery algorithm.
end note

== O. Prometheus pulls only a captured publication view ==
Prom -[#1565C0]> App : [call] GET /metrics (one in-flight request allowed)
App -[#1565C0]> Store : [call] OTel observable callback: Capture() once
Store --[#388E3C]> App : [result] immutable publications + copied failure state\nand one captured time At
App -[#7B1FA2]> App : [decision] Valid(evidence): reason, failed dependencies, expiry\nformat gauges and custom labels
App --[#388E3C]> Prom : [result] pod_workload_info=1 with component/instance/group\nworkload_status: Running=1, Initializing=1, seven others=0\ncreated_timestamp only while its proof is valid
note over App,Prom
Full metric names start with karta_. Status and Pod rows carry observation_valid=true/false.
Invalid known rows can remain visible with false. Workload failure adds observation_valid health=0.
Scraping makes no Kubernetes request and runs no JQ or CEL.
A captured view is consistent at Capture(); a later invalidation affects the next capture.
end note
Prom -[#1565C0]> App : [call] GET /readyz after source synchronization
App -[#1565C0]> Runtime : [call] Ready()
Runtime --[#388E3C]> App : [result] Pod + selected namespace/Karta sources + RequiredKinds\nready, without error and not past verification maxAge?
App --[#388E3C]> Prom : [result] 200 if required source gate passes; otherwise 503
note over Runtime,Inventory
Readiness is not workload readiness. An optional selected kind can fail without blocking /readyz.
Resource-type observation health still reports that failure.
end note

